  "notes": [
    "<sandbox>/work in argv stands for a scratch copy of the files listed in inputs, mounted read-only; runs/RUN-lean-stuck/inputs/ holds those files as they ran.",
    "Recorded for W1 follow-up 1 (docs/waves/W1-report.md). run@1's task field admits only W<n>-S<nn>/W<n>-T<nn> IDs, so the follow-up is named in task_label instead.",
    "Each log is the container's stdout and stderr, as lean printed them. verdict_lines are the error and warning header lines, the #print axioms lines and the #eval/#check output lines, copied from the log.",
    "OddCheck.lean is S3.L1's AST block followed by its cell 2, verbatim; BalanceStuck.lean is S3.L4's lean block verbatim.",
    "guard-stuck adds one theorem (authored) for the configuration S3.L4's cell 1 calls with typing bypassed: the guard `balance(30) >= 30` as `.ge (.bal (.num 30)) (.num 30)` has no step.",
    "S3.L4's cell 1 itself is text notation for the trace view (INS-interp), which no engine reads yet; this record covers it through the Lean relation in the same lesson.",
    "Re-executed on 2026-10-27 with scripts/runs/rerun-argv.mjs, from the same argv and the same staged inputs, after edits to the lessons it cites left their code blocks unchanged; every log matched the earlier recording byte for byte."
